# Design bar

- One clear reading ritual: prose and code stay visually linked (hover, scroll-sync, or anchors)—never two unrelated columns.
- Comfortable long-read: generous measure for prose, readable code pane, restrained chrome.
- Distinct type pairing; limited palette with one accent; consistent spacing scale.
- Motion only when it clarifies the mapping between text and code.
- Every screen should feel intentional at a glance.
